// 7159
[enum_7159]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=1,If a westerner has met a sea singer, soothsayer or siren, it was likely here; it is a minor centre of study and research for those not enamoured of the civilised east.
val=2,The sea in the area is teeming with fish and turtles, making it a favourite for whales. One named 'Shuma' is particularly storied.
val=3,A merchant island, where westerners mingle with easterners. The slave trade begins here.
val=4,The village of Gongdung is here. They are particularly suspicious of anything inhuman: soothsayers, sirens, etc.
val=5,One large and one small island divided by a wide strip of water shallow enough to wade. Its Khan rules from the northern isle.
val=6,Legend has it that this island chain was a trio of giant sea turtles, turned to stone by unknown forces. Largely uninhabited.
val=7,Only known home of the eastern cyclops: a race of semi-sentient humanoids who get on well with everyone.
val=8,One of the larger eastern islands. Produces gunpowder which is traded with the rest of the Wushanko Isles, and also grows apples. The ruling khan is territorial and hostile towards all westerners.
val=9,The island of Hanto is ruled by a tyrannical khan who has closed his borders to trade. As a result, smuggling is rife in the area.
val=10,A thin strip of land nestled in shallow, warm seas. Mermaids have been known to visit this place in large numbers.
val=11,Sulphur is mined here, and gunpowder is made. At the island's height is a massive jade palace, built by Thalassia's khan.
val=12,Houses several fishing towns that make strong use of explosives in their fishing. The ruling khan is known to be cruel, especially to his own people.
val=13,The only major concentration of the seatouched people, a reasonably fertile island with a single, semi-fortified township.
val=14,A living island (likely an evolved sea monster) with a brain at its centre and floating eyeballs as its sensory system.
val=15,An island curiously shaped like the shell of a nautilus. Home of a siren seasinger.
val=16,Vast columns of black stone erupt from the ground across the length of this island; one can walk from coast to coast without ever touching the soil.
val=17,Honazo, a crabbing town, stands in a wide and peaceful bay here.
val=18,The scientific and superstitious disagree on what came to form the knuckle-shaped depressions indenting the entire surface of this island.
val=19,Named not for their shape or anything that goes on there, but for the proliferation of waterfalls that fill the air with mist and spray.
val=20,The sea between these two islands is an unfathomable depth, a rift of stone from which earthquakes are born.
val=21,A mining colony originally built to dig for black slate; it has become highly prosperous since discovering large quantities of high-quality gems.
val=22,The Chimera Isles are here. Since the straits are used by smugglers, a number of inns and smuggling dens can be found on the isles.
val=23,This is where aging sea monsters go to die. Vast bones scatter the coral outcrops as they plunge to the depths.
val=24,Swift currents, strong winds and a remarkably stable microclimate make the average temperature of this island lower than its neighbours. Rumours exist of a Purist movement having made it their headquarters.
val=25,The island of Haranu is awash with cherry forests. The island was once home to occultists before they were rounded up and executed by the Scythe's khans.
val=26,This is an area renowned for its hospitality and hot springs. Beyond the odd cave giant, the island chain is a paradise.
val=27,This large island is the home of the soothsayers, where they are educated before they practice their arts elsewhere.
val=28,This is a narrow pass that has been the scene of many battles. It is now used by jade traders.
val=29,An island mentioned in whispers as a place where the mind is made sharper, the senses clearer and meditation more effective.
val=30,The prevailing winds around this island change daily, some say on the whim of the sea witches who live here.
val=31,An island renowned for its geishas, as well as hibiscus gardens and beautiful scenery.
val=32,Declared taboo for settlement by an ancient khan; now overgrown with juniper groves and a rare haven for land-dwelling beasts.
val=33,Training islands for the Death Lotus assassins. It is also pockmarked with fishing villages, which form a useful cover.
val=34,A cave network made bright by large outcrops of quartz and salt. Home to Shuma the whale.
val=35,The people of Kei Pi are renowned for their energy and their hedonism, although some say that the vicious group of pirates known as the Pin operate out of a hidden base here.
val=36,The pirates of this island have an unusual reputation for decency.
val=37,The only known growing location of a medicinal herb of vast potency.
val=38,A fishing village built on stilts. Once home to the Whaler; since obliterated. Still home to the Old Man of the Sea, who can psychically link to sea monsters.
val=39,An outpost of the khans' power, heavily fortified. Serves as a centre of frontier justice and bureaucracy.
val=40,The most populous city of all the Eastern Lands. The city is largely built on the coast, with some smaller buildings built into a mountain.
val=41,The diplomatic capital of the Eastern Lands, and the site of the Halls of Reckoning.
val=42,On this island stands a great hole that has never been explored. Pirates dump bodies here.
val=43,Officially accorded neutral ground, this island is a place of peace. Khans can relax here, if nowhere else.
val=44,A heavily fortified island known for the refinement and ambition of its citizens.
val=45,A major cultural centre and focus of social gathering.
val=46,Headquarters and stronghold of the Death Lotus assassins.
val=47,Home of Quin, the sea singer. A small island, surrounded by sea monsters, with jungle and a single palace on four white pillars.
val=48,Rumour abounds of a tiny island where two beast-headed sorcerers bind the drowned dead to their service.
default=

// 7160
[enum_7160]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=2,The sea in the area is teeming with fish and turtles, making it a favourite for whales. Here, Shuma attacked and stranded the Whaler.
val=11,Sulphur is mined here, and gunpowder is made. At the island's height is a massive jade palace, built by Thalassia's Khan before he was killed by the Assassin.
val=17,Honazo, a crabbing town, stood in a wide and peaceful bay here. It has been largely destroyed by Shuma.
val=19,Named not for their shape or anything that goes on there, but for the proliferation of waterfalls that fill the air with mist and spray. The Missionary sunk the Pride of Chaos here.
val=24,Swift currents, strong winds and a remarkably stable microclimate make the average temperature of this island lower than its neighbours. The Missionary discovered a Purist group's headquarters here.
val=25,The island of Haranu is awash with cherry forests. The island was once home to occultists before they were rounded up and executed by the Scythe's Khans; a renegade group returned to the island only to be outed by the Convict.
val=26,This is an area renowned for its hospitality and hot springs. Beyond the odd cave giant, the island is a paradise. Wu was killed here by the Assassin.
val=28,This is a narrow pass that has been the scene of many battles. It is now used by jade trawlers. Here the Whaler tried to set a blockade against Shuma.
val=31,An island renowned for its geishas, as well as hibiscus gardens and beautiful scenery. Oshoru was khan of this island before his death at the Occultist's hands.
val=32,Declared taboo for settlement by an ancient khan; now overgrown with juniper groves and a rare haven for land-dwelling beasts. Home only to the mercenary group known as the Lost Men.
val=34,A cave network made bright by large outcrops of quartz and salt. Once home to the mighty Shuma.
val=36,The pirates of this island have an unusual reputation for decency. They are loyal to Kirau, informer and fence to the Assassin.
val=42,On this island stands a great hole that has never been explored. Pirates dump bodies here, and the Occultist sought death within.
default=

